### Triangulation script per core (Task 2)
```ps1
# For each core in m0plus,m3,m4,m33:
.\tools\qemu\triangulate.ps1 -Elf tools/renode/out/bench-m0plus.elf -QemuLog tools/qemu/qemu-m0plus.log
.\tools\qemu\triangulate.ps1 -Elf tools/renode/out/bench-m3.elf     -QemuLog tools/qemu/qemu-m3.log
.\tools\qemu\triangulate.ps1 -Elf tools/renode/out/bench-m4.elf     -QemuLog tools/qemu/qemu-m4.log
.\tools\qemu\triangulate.ps1 -Elf tools/renode/out/bench-m33.elf    -QemuLog tools/qemu/qemu-m33.log
# System-mode args inside script:
#   qemu-system-arm -M mps2-an385 -nographic -kernel <elf> -d instr -D <log> -semihosting
#   then: (Get-Content <log> | Measure-Object -Line).Lines  -> instr total
#         instr/byte = instr / (1024*25), instr/record est for 32 B
# User-mode alternative: qemu-arm -d instr -D <log> <elf>
```

### Proxy fallback — static instruction count via objdump (QEMU not available)
```ps1
$objdump = "C:\Program Files (x86)\GNU Arm Embedded Toolchain\10 2021.10\bin\arm-none-eabi-objdump.exe"
$size    = "C:\Program Files (x86)\GNU Arm Embedded Toolchain\10 2021.10\bin\arm-none-eabi-size.exe"
# per ELF:
& $objdump -d tools/renode/out/bench-m0plus.elf | Select-String -Pattern "^\s*[0-9a-f]+\s*:" | Measure-Object  # static instr count
& $size -A -d tools/renode/out/bench-m0plus.elf   # section sizes
& $size -B tools/renode/out/bench-m0plus.elf      # dec/hex summary
# Repeat for bench-m3.elf, bench-m4.elf, bench-m33.elf, bench-m0plus-sizeopt.elf, bench-m3-sizeopt.elf
```

